     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, or 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. The maximum single dose is typically 850 mg to 1,000 mg. This order is about twice the daily limit. It carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals.**\n- **1700 mg total daily**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily, if the 1700 was meant as a daily total.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want. If 1700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed it."
      }
     ],
